// @run
// @log 1
// @log 1.5
// @log -2.25
// @log 0.5
// `f32.load` — an f32 read out of raw bytes written as i32 words. Every constant
// is an EXACT binary float (a power-of-two-scaled dyadic rational), so the
// printed decimal is exact and the case pins the load, not the formatter:
//
//   0x3F800000 =  1.0     0x3FC00000 =  1.5
//   0xC0100000 = -2.25    0x3F000000 =  0.5
//
// This is the shape webcraft's port needs: a column of f32s laid down as bytes
// and read back at f32 width. Bit patterns derived with python `struct`.
//
// 0xC0100000 has its top bit set and is written here as itself: a hex literal is
// a bit pattern of its destination's width, and `__store_i32__`'s parameter is
// the destination. At i32 width the pattern denotes -1072693248.
__store_i32__(0, 0x3F800000)
print(__load_f32__(0))
__store_i32__(4, 0x3FC00000)
print(__load_f32__(4))
__store_i32__(8, 0xC0100000)
print(__load_f32__(8))
__store_i32__(12, 0x3F000000)
print(__load_f32__(12))
